  "prefLabel": "En 607.04 System Maps",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "En 607.04 System Maps.\n\n(a) Each water utility shall have on file at its principal office located within New Hampshire a map, maps, or drawings showing the following:\n\n(1) The size, character, and location of all mains including hydrants and valves;\n\n(2) The size and location of each service connection, where practicable; and\n\n(3) The layout of all principal pumping stations, filter, and chlorinating plants to show size, location, and character of all major equipment, pipelines, connections, valves, and other equipment used.\n\n(b) In lieu of showing service locations on maps, referred to in (a)(2) above, a card record or other suitable means may be used.\n\nSource. #13911, eff 3-21-24 (see Revision Note at chapter heading for En 600)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/en600.html"
